screens.summary:
Gantt with one column per business day. Padding 28 48 24. There is a 280px label column, and the chart width W is measured with a ResizeObserver (1456px at 1920).

Top bar:
- Eyebrow 'Timeline'. Title 'Three months' / 'Two weeks'.
- Mono subtitle: '28 Sep 2026 – 15 Jan 2027 · 77 business days', or '5 Oct – 16 Oct · 10 business days' in 2w.
- Legend: BAU, Project, Past target, Previous plan, Milestone, Target, Overload.
- Pan controls: 32x32 chevrons plus 'This week'. Visible in 2w only.
- Zoom segmented control '2 weeks | 3 months'. A sliding ink pill 96px wide, positioned at left 3px or 99px.

Zoom windows:
- 3m: T0 Mon 28 Sep to T1 Fri 15 Jan. That is 77 BD columns plus 15 gap slivers of 5px each. Weekends and holidays collapse into one sliver per run.
- 2w: 10 BDs (Mon of the current week plus wk×7), with 18px slivers. wk is clamped to [-1, 13].

Chart rows:
- Date header, 80px, four tiers:
  - months: 13/600, label pinned when clamped, hidden if narrower than 70px;
  - ISO weeks 'W41' in mono 10;
  - day pills: '5' in 3m or 'Mon 5' in 2w; today is inverted ink;
  - BD numbers: '3' / 'BD3'; BD1 in ink.
- Capacity row, 76px, caption 'Hours per day against 8h. Notched = BAU, solid = project.':
  - one vertical stack per BD at 5px/hour, with a dashed 8h line at bottom 51px;
  - BAU notches use a repeating gradient of 4px fill and 1px gap;
  - projects use a soft fill with an accent outline;
  - overload turns red with a one-shot pulse;
  - tag 'FI move · Mon 4 Jan'.
- Lanes (scroll area). Group header 40px; BAU row 38px; rotation row 48px; project row 64px.
  - 'Private Credit · BAU': one tick per occurrence, 4px wide in 3m. In 2w it is wide with text 'Returns · 6h'. After the move or once handed over, it is drawn outlined.
  - 'Private Credit · Projects'.
  - 'Fixed Income · BAU': the 'Eurozone sovereign rotation 4h/day' row. Segments are Build (solid, soft fill) or Refresh (dashed). Codes show in 3m, 'Germany · Build' in 2w. Note: 'Starts Mon 4 Jan with Germany, first Build pass →'.
  - 'Fixed Income · Projects'.
- Project row, left side: name, a Roll of the forecast date, and a delta chip.
- Project row, right side, layered:
  - ghost of the previous plan (dashed, opacity 0.55);
  - forecast bar;
  - risk overrun from target to forecast;
  - milestone diamonds (filled once passed);
  - forecast end diamond;
  - target Γ marker;
  - flash ghost end diamond plus 'was 27 Nov';
  - 'moved +N BD' chip;
  - off-range label 'Target Late Mar 2027 →'.
  - Define status draws a hatched bar.
- Overlay lines: today (1px ink) and the FI move (1.5px fi-accent).
- Footnote: 'Weekends and UK bank holidays are collapsed to slivers. Hover a row to trace it through the capacity strip; click for details.'

Hover and tooltip:
- Hovering a row sets the global hover; everything else dims to 0.28.
- A 300px cursor tooltip is positioned imperatively. Variants: day, routine, rotation, project, milestone.

Clicking a project row opens a 460px side panel (no scrim). It contains:
- domain chip and close button;
- name, and the goal in serif 24px;
- facts: Forecast, Target, Against target, Confidence 'N of 5', Last check-in;
- milestone list;
- 'Open workspace' and 'Tell Remi' buttons.

Zoom and pan re-lay out every element with 440ms spring transitions.

engineAlgorithms.spec:
remi.v1 shape:
- projects[] in stored shape;
- tasks {id: bool}; doneOn {id: ISO};
- feed[] (its 'when' is a display string);
- funds bool[12] (today's r-ret run); routines[];
- bauDone {'rid:ISO': ISO};
- notes {ISO: [{id, t: 'HH:MM', text}]};
- m2: true.
Migration m2 inserts man-0 into manco now[0] if it is missing.

Mapping:
- Project fields map to the entity tables. Now blocks become now-horizon milestones with their tasks. Next items become next-horizon milestones. Explicit milestones are kept.
- 'ov' becomes HourOverride. scope from/to 'D Mon' strings must be resolved to ISO dates in the right year.
- checkins become CheckIn records.
- tasks and doneOn become task done flags and doneAt.
- bauDone becomes RoutineRun rows. funds becomes RunChecklistTick rows for r-ret on the import-day occurrence.
- Note t becomes createdAt = day + t in the local timezone.
- Feed 'when' values are unrecoverable; use the import time.

Textbook: sections, pages (tree via parent), blocks, and chart html strings → ChartAsset. The src marker 'charts/price-yield.html' maps to the bundled sample.
